# Graph-admission verifier scratch (A2-294c). verify.py writes its captured verifier outputs and two
# ~2 MB RelationshipGraph dumps here. Pointing --verifier-out at this path is what makes the
# receipt's output_ref repo-relative and stable for a human reader instead of a worker's /tmp. The
# bytes themselves are NOT committed, and that is forced, not chosen: they are a function of the
# head (v-contract-diff names the commit; the type-check listings name the export dir), while
# GATEORDER-0 `trailing_record_commits` admits only the receipt file and a declared derived artefact
# into a commit after the receipt's head. Committing them therefore refuses as CHANGE_SET_INCOMPLETE
# no matter how the commits are ordered -- measured on this branch at 76cc7ab (C06, both locally and
# in CI run 36089950017). Recorded here so the next agent does not rediscover it by going red.
receipts/graph/verifier-out/
